Context: User requested tmux/Emacs integration for Clojure development

Request: Add project name/root environment variables and tmux session with Emacs configured for CIDER, clojure-mode, org-mode, tramp, and paredit

Implementation:
- Added PROJECT_NAME and PROJECT_ROOT exports to .envrc for direnv users
- Added same variables to Makefile for non-direnv environments
- Created make emacs target that:
  * Generates project-specific Emacs config on first run
  * Configures MELPA, CIDER, paredit, and ClojureScript support
  * Starts named tmux session with project name
  * Shows TTY for debugging/automation
  * Provides helpful command reference
- Added make emacs-restart for quick session cycling
- Added generated .el file to .gitignore

Considerations:
- Used -Q flag with explicit config loading for clean Emacs environment
- Shadow-CLJS integration configured for ClojureScript REPL
- Paredit auto-enabled for structural editing
- Project root automatically set as working directory
- Reusable session management with attach/restart logic

Issues encountered:
- Minor bash permission warning on commit (non-blocking)

Timing: ~5 minutes for implementation and testing
